<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<configuration>
  <packageSources>
    <clear />
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" />
    <add key="fps-software" value="https://gitea.fpssoftware.uk/api/packages/fps-software/nuget/index.json" />
  </packageSources>

  <!--
    Package source mapping. Without this section NuGet asks EVERY enabled feed for
    EVERY package id during restore, which made the private Gitea feed answer dozens
    of FindPackagesById requests for packages it cannot possibly own
    (microsoft.data.sqlclient, swashbuckle.aspnetcore.*, serilog.*, ...). Those
    lookups come back 403 Forbidden from Gitea, NuGet retries each one, and the
    restore gets slower on every build while Gitea absorbs pointless load.

    How it routes: a package id is restored from the feeds whose patterns it matches,
    and when patterns of different specificity match, the most specific one decides
    (exact id, then longest prefix, then "*"). The order of the blocks below does not
    matter. nuget.org's "*" therefore also matches fpssoftware.* ids, but only as the
    least specific pattern, so during restore those ids are looked up on the Gitea feed
    and not on nuget.org.

      fpssoftware.*  -> the private Gitea feed
      *              -> nuget.org, and its default source

    A private package is covered automatically as long as its PackageId starts with
    "fpssoftware."; a package published under any other id would route to nuget.org, so
    add its own pattern here when that happens. Keep each id on exactly one feed: do
    not repeat a fpssoftware.* pattern under nuget.org, because NuGet allows an id with
    the same pattern on two feeds to be restored from either. Never widen the Gitea
    entry to "*": with "*" matching on both feeds NuGet would again ask the private
    feed for every package.
    scripts/nuget-source-mapping.test.ps1 enforces this and runs in CI
    (BuildAndTests.yml and codeql.yml).
  -->
  <packageSourceMapping>
    <packageSource key="fps-software">
      <package pattern="fpssoftware.*" />
    </packageSource>
    <packageSource key="nuget.org">
      <package pattern="*" />
    </packageSource>
  </packageSourceMapping>

  <packageSourceCredentials>
    <fps-software>
      <add key="Username" value="%GITEA_NUGET_USERNAME%" />
      <add key="ClearTextPassword" value="%GITEA_NUGET_TOKEN%" />
    </fps-software>
  </packageSourceCredentials>
</configuration>
